<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
ALIS project-local UnrealBuildTool config (SOT).

This file is the source of truth. It is materialized into
Saved/UnrealBuildTool/BuildConfiguration.xml by Sync-UBTConfig.ps1, which is
invoked at the start of packaging/build entry points so that periodic Saved/
clean-ups do not lose the throttle settings.

UBT reads <ProjectRoot>/Saved/UnrealBuildTool/BuildConfiguration.xml when
invoked with project context (BuildCookRun -project=...) and gives it highest
precedence among static XmlConfig paths. See Engine source:
  Engine/Source/Programs/UnrealBuildTool/System/XmlConfig.cs:120-130

Why these values (cold-build OOM fix, 2026-04-27):
  MemoryPerActionBytes = 4 GiB
    Matches observed UE 5.7 SharedPCH peak in monolithic Shipping. The UE
    default 1.5 GiB is stale and was the OOM driver in our cold packaging
    (cl.exe C3859 / C1076 / Windows commit code 1455).
  ProcessorCountMultiplier = 1.0 (default)
    Values >1.0 oversubscribe cl.exe and remove the only OOM safety net.
  bAllCores = false (default)
    Uses physical cores only. With 4 GiB/action throttle this yields ~14-15
    parallel cl.exe on a 64 GB machine and fits with OS headroom.

Do NOT add UnrealBuildAccelerator tuning here without a separate measured
cause; UBA is an acceleration layer, not a memory-pressure fix.
-->
<Configuration xmlns="https://www.unrealengine.com/BuildConfiguration">
  <BuildConfiguration>
    <bAllCores>false</bAllCores>
  </BuildConfiguration>

  <ParallelExecutor>
    <ProcessorCountMultiplier>1.0</ProcessorCountMultiplier>
    <MemoryPerActionBytes>4294967296</MemoryPerActionBytes>
  </ParallelExecutor>
</Configuration>
